{
  // Dependency-vulnerability gate for CI (replaces the bare `npm audit --audit-level=high`,
  // which has no way to record a reasoned exception).
  //
  // The gate stays sharp: anything high/critical that is NOT listed below fails the build.
  // `allowlist` is per-advisory (GHSA id), never per-severity — we do not lower the level.
  //
  // Adding an entry requires, in this file: (1) the advisory id, (2) why it does not apply to
  // THIS codebase, measured — not assumed, (3) an expiry date, (4) what removes the need for it.
  // An expired entry is a task, not a renewal: re-check it, do not extend it by reflex.
  //
  // Policy: docs/development/dependency-audit.md
  "$schema": "https://github.com/IBM/audit-ci/raw/main/docs/schema.json",
  "moderate": false,
  "high": true,
  "critical": true,
  "allowlist": [
    // GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 — react-router "RSC Mode CSRF Bypass Allows Action Execution Before
    // 400 Response" (high). Vulnerable range 7.12.0–8.2.0; there is NO fix in the 7.x line
    // (react-router-dom stops at 7.18.1; the fix is react-router v8 >= 8.2.1, a different
    // package and a breaking upgrade). Every other react-router advisory in this tree IS fixed
    // — 7.18.1 closes the open-redirect, XSS, SSR-hydration and route-matching DoS ones.
    //
    // Why it does not apply here (measured 2026-07-29): the suite apex shell is a **static SPA
    // built by Vite** and copied into the Apache document root by the Dockerfile's frontend
    // stage — there is no Node server in the image at all. `src/app/router.tsx` uses
    // `createBrowserRouter` with **element-only** routes: grepping the tree finds no route
    // `action:` / `loader:` key, no `@react-router/dev`, no `react-router/server`, no
    // `createStaticHandler`, no RSC entry, and no server-side render/hydrate call. The
    // advisory's attack path (a server executing a route action before returning 400) has no
    // counterpart in a client-only bundle.
    //
    // Expiry: 2026-08-31. Removed by the react-router v8 migration wave (bundled with the
    // NENE2 RR8 re-evaluation). If that wave slips past the expiry, the entry must be
    // re-argued in a PR — not silently extended.
    "GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2",

    // GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg — brace-expansion "DoS via unbounded expansion length causing an
    // out-of-memory process crash" (high). Fixed in 5.0.8, which this tree DOES take at the
    // top level (see `overrides` in package.json). What remains are the copies nested under
    // `minimatch@3` (eslint-plugin-import, eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y → brace-expansion 1.1.16)
    // and under `minimatch@5` (@redocly/openapi-core → 2.1.3).
    //
    // Why they are not force-upgraded (measured 2026-07-29): a blanket
    // `"brace-expansion": "^5.0.8"` override hoists v5 into `minimatch@3`, whose CommonJS
    // `require('brace-expansion')` expects the module itself to be the function. v5 exports
    // `{ expand }` instead, so the call throws `expand is not a function` — verified in this
    // tree by requiring `eslint-plugin-import/node_modules/minimatch` and matching a brace
    // pattern (throws under the blanket override, passes under the scoped one). `npm run lint`
    // happens not to reach that code path today, which makes the blanket override a latent
    // landmine rather than a safe fix. The override is therefore scoped to `brace-expansion@5`.
    //
    // Why the residue does not apply here (measured 2026-07-29): the affected copies are
    // **dev-only**. `npm ls --omit=dev --all brace-expansion` is empty, as is the same query
    // for `minimatch` and `js-yaml` — none of them reach the shipped bundle. The consumers are
    // lint plugins and the OpenAPI codegen, fed by repo-authored patterns in CI, not by
    // attacker-controlled input.
    //
    // Expiry: 2026-08-31. The removal condition is a **resolution fact, not a release name**:
    // this entry goes away when `eslint-plugin-import` and `eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y` stop
    // resolving `minimatch@3`, and `@redocly/openapi-core` stops resolving `minimatch@5` —
    // i.e. when `tests/toolchain/brace-expansion-override.test.ts` finds only copies that a
    // flat `brace-expansion@^5` override would not break. Re-argue, do not extend.
    "GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg",
  ],
}
